      "content": "okay but if the \"historical tradition\" is the only metric that counts, then any law based on modern technology or current public safety needs is basically dead on arrival in court. shouldn't we just admit that the current legal framework has essentially prioritized a specific historical interpretation over the government's ability to actually manage modern risks?",
